{
  "_comment": [
    "Test files under backend/tests that neither runner executes.",
    "",
    "vitest.config.unit.js includes tests/**/*.unit.test.js; jest.config.js",
    "matches **/tests/integration/**/*.test.js. A file named *.test.js outside",
    "tests/integration/ matches neither, so it never runs and nothing reports",
    "that it did not \u2014 the suite prints a healthy pass count without it.",
    "",
    "These are not dead code. tests/studyAnalyticsService.test.js was in this",
    "state, and renaming it into the vitest glob made it fail immediately on a",
    "real timezone defect in the service it covers. Every entry here is a test",
    "someone wrote that has never protected anything.",
    "",
    "They are listed rather than renamed in bulk because bringing 94 suites",
    "into CI at once means triaging whatever they find, and most of them need a",
    "live PostgreSQL. Renaming them without reading them would either turn CI",
    "red or, worse, tempt someone to delete the ones that fail.",
    "",
    "This list is a ceiling, not a target: scripts/check-test-discovery.js fails",
    "on any new undiscovered test file, and on any entry here that has since",
    "been wired up or removed. Delete entries as they are brought in."
  ],
